      "title": "UBER: The $10B FCF Inflection and the \"Utilization Arbitrage\" the market is missing.",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "January 2026",
      "summary": "The author argues that Wall Street is underestimating Uber's shift into an asset-light tollbooth for autonomous vehicle fleets, where transferring depreciation, insurance, and maintenance to hardware partners increases net profit per ride from $2.37 to $3.90. Supported by $10.1B in projected FY2026 operating cash flow, high-margin advertising growth, and Pershing Square's accumulation in the mid-$70s setting a price floor, Uber is framed as a high-margin utility with an expanding FCF yield.",
      "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/ValueInvesting/search/?q=UBER&restrict_sr=1&sort=top",
      "btn_label": "Reddit DDs \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Unit Economics of Uber: Where Every $100 Ride Goes",
      "fund": "Substack / Thesis Rationale",
      "date": "October 2025",
      "summary": "This deep dive breaks down the unit economics of a $100 Uber ride, analyzing how $70 goes to driver payouts, $10 to incentives, and the remaining margin flows into platform leverage. The thesis models a base-case fair value of $80\u2013$90 per share and a bull case of $110\u2013$130+ driven by 12\u201315% annual FCF growth, cross-selling delivery/freight, and operating margin expansion.",
      "url": "https://thesisrationale.substack.com/p/the-unit-economics-of-uber-where",
      "btn_label": "Substack Memo \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "Everyone's debating whether AVs will kill Uber(UBER). The real story is more nuanced",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "March 2026",
      "summary": "This 10-step institutional analysis evaluates Uber's underlying cash generation, identifying that true owner earnings are closer to $4.1B after stripping out accrued insurance reserves rather than headline FCF figures. The author highlights driver reclassification and state labor laws as more immediate risks than autonomous vehicles, while noting Uber's fleet utilization advantage positions it well to capture AV upside at a fair valuation.",
